  "step_3": "The decision reason requires identifying outcomes with probability > 1/n, where n is the number of outcomes. In A (n=2), only 0 Euros (75%) is probable (since 75% > 50%). In B (n=3), only 0 Euros (50%) is probable (since 50% > 33.3%). Thus, both have exactly one probable outcome, so average number of probable outcomes is equal (1). The reason is indifferent, and does not prefer either. However, the individual does not mention this formal categorization. Instead, they compare the chance of winning something (positive amount), which is 25% in A and 50% in B. This is a different criterion — not about probable outcomes as defined in the reason. The individual does not refer to the threshold (1/n), nor does their justification involve computing or evaluating probable outcomes. Therefore, the individual did not use the decision reason as specified. The justification is based on a different principle (chance of winning something), not on the average number of probable outcomes. Hence, the decision reason was not used.",
